{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"title":"Getting Started with AstronomyKit","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to add AstronomyKit to your project and perform basic astronomical calculations."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers"],"title":"Essentials"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit provides a type-safe Swift interface for astronomical calculations. This article walks you through installation and your first calculations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Installation","type":"heading","anchor":"Installation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add AstronomyKit to your Swift package:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["dependencies: [","    .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/AstronomyKit\", from: \"3.0.0\")","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Or in Xcode: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"File → Add Package Dependencies"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" and enter the repository URL.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Your First Calculations","type":"heading","anchor":"Your-First-Calculations"},{"level":3,"text":"Import the Package","type":"heading","anchor":"Import-the-Package"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import AstronomyKit"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Set Up Your Observer Location","type":"heading","anchor":"Set-Up-Your-Observer-Location"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most astronomical calculations require an observer location on Earth:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ New York City","let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7128, longitude: -74.0060)","","\/\/ With elevation (in meters)","let denver = Observer(latitude: 39.7392, longitude: -104.9903, height: 1609)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Get the Current Time","type":"heading","anchor":"Get-the-Current-Time"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for all time-based calculations:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Current time","let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ From a specific date","let newYear = AstroTime(year: 2025, month: 1, day: 1, hour: 12)","","\/\/ From Foundation Date","let fromDate = AstroTime(Date())"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Calculate a Position","anchor":"Calculate-a-Position","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Find where a celestial body appears in your sky:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Mars in the local sky","let mars = try CelestialBody.mars.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)","print(\"Altitude: \\(mars.altitude)°\")     \/\/ Height above horizon","print(\"Direction: \\(mars.compassDirection)\")  \/\/ N, NE, E, etc."],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Find the Moon Phase","anchor":"Find-the-Moon-Phase","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let angle = try Moon.phaseAngle(at: .now)","print(\"\\(Moon.emoji(for: angle)) \\(Moon.phaseName(for: angle))\")","\/\/ Output: 🌔 Waxing Gibbous"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Get Rise and Set Times","anchor":"Get-Rise-and-Set-Times","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if let sunrise = try CelestialBody.sun.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Sunrise: \\(sunrise.date)\")","}","","if let sunset = try CelestialBody.sun.setTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Sunset: \\(sunset.date)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Error Handling","anchor":"Error-Handling","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All potentially failing calculations throw ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["do {","    let position = try CelestialBody.earth.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)","} catch AstronomyError.earthNotAllowed {","    print(\"Cannot observe Earth from Earth!\")","} catch {","    print(\"Calculation failed: \\(error)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for time scales and observer locations"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialPositions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for positions and velocities of any body"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonPhases","isActive":true},{"text":" for phases, quarters, libration, and nodes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift bindings for Don Cross’ "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" library."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"AstronomyKit","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit","type":"topic"},"https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","title":"Astronomy Engine","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Astronomy Engine"}]},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/TimeAndObservers":{"url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/timeandobservers","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Time and Observers","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Work with astronomical time and geographic observer locations."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers","role":"article"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime":{"url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime","title":"AstroTime","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represents a moment in time for astronomical calculations."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AstroTime","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AstroTime"}]},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstronomyError":{"url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astronomyerror","title":"AstronomyError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Errors that can occur during astronomy calculations."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AstronomyError"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AstronomyError"}]},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/MoonPhases":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Calculate moon phases, quarter